      "id": "2122485785396236711",
      "lang": "en",
      "note_tweet": {
        "text": "Free access for 200,000 scientists is a big scale-up, and pairing it with training and support matters — access alone doesn't close the gap for researchers without AI experience. Two questions: how will selection avoid concentrating access in already well-resourced institutions, and will the Nov. 23 application prioritise researchers in under-resourced regions or fields? The default not to train on shared data is also an important trust signal."
      },
